<main>

<section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview">
  <div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal">
      <span class="ey">How It Works</span>
      <h1>From PunchOut to invoice. Six simple steps.</h1>
      <p class="lead">See exactly how a buyer moves from procurement into your catalog, gets approval, sends a PO and creates the final store order.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__actions">
        <a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Connect my first buyer <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn secbtn" href="#details">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="page-proofline">
        <span><b>✓</b> Free Integration</span>
        <span><b>✓</b> Cancel anytime</span>
        <span><b>✓</b> No transaction fees</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="hero-visual reveal">
      <div class="hero-visual__label"><span>PunchOut Central</span><b>Connected</b></div>
      <div class="visual-flow"><div class="visual-step is-accent"><i>01</i><span><strong>PunchOut Started</strong><small>Buyer enters catalog</small></span><em>01</em></div><div class="visual-step is-lavender"><i>02</i><span><strong>Cart Returned</strong><small>Cart goes back</small></span><em>02</em></div><div class="visual-step is-peach"><i>03</i><span><strong>Buyer Approved</strong><small>Internal approval</small></span><em>03</em></div><div class="visual-step is-lime"><i>04</i><span><strong>PO Received</strong><small>Approved PO arrives</small></span><em>04</em></div><div class="visual-step "><i>05</i><span><strong>Store Order Created</strong><small>Shopify order created</small></span><em>05</em></div><div class="visual-step is-accent"><i>06</i><span><strong>Invoice Generated</strong><small>Transaction completed</small></span><em>06</em></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="trust-strip" aria-label="PunchOut Central credibility">
  <div class="wrap trust-strip__inner">
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">★</span><div><strong>Trustpilot 4.7+</strong><span>Customer rating</span></div></div>
    <span class="trust-strip__divider"></span>
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">PPAI</span><div><strong>PPAI Member</strong><span>Promotional products industry</span></div></div>
    <span class="trust-strip__divider"></span>
    <div class="trust-strip__item"><span class="trust-strip__icon">S</span><div><strong>Shopify Partner</strong><span>Commerce experience</span></div></div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="sec" id="details">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">The full journey</span><h2>One connected order. Six clear steps.</h2><p class="lead">Each step has one job, and PunchOut Central keeps them linked.</p></div>
    <div class="simple-steps"><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">01</span><h3>PunchOut Started</h3><p>Buyer opens your Shopify catalog from procurement.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">02</span><h3>Cart Returned</h3><p>The selected cart returns to their procurement system.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">03</span><h3>Buyer Approved</h3><p>The buyer completes their internal approval process.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">04</span><h3>PO Received</h3><p>PunchOut Central receives the approved purchase order.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">05</span><h3>Store Order Created</h3><p>The matching Shopify order is created automatically.</p></article><article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">06</span><h3>Invoice Generated</h3><p>Invoice activity stays tied to the buyer, PO and order.</p></article></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="rule">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">The important rule</span><h2>Cart return is not the final order.</h2><p class="lead">The ecommerce order should be created after the approved PO, not when the buyer simply returns the cart.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">01</span><h3>Cart ≠ order</h3><p>Returning a cart sends a requisition back to procurement for approval.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">02</span><h3>PO = approval signal</h3><p>The approved purchase order is what moves the transaction forward.</p></article><article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">03</span><h3>One correlation chain</h3><p>Gateway, session, cart, PO, store order and invoice stay connected.</p></article></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="proof">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Built for trust</span><h2>Proven enough for the customer you cannot afford to lose.</h2><p class="lead">Simple on the surface. Dependable underneath.</p></div>
    <div class="metrics-row">
      <article class="metric reveal"><strong>90+</strong><span>customers use PunchOut technology built by our team.</span></article>
      <article class="metric reveal"><strong>$50M+</strong><span>in order value processed through our technology every year.</span></article>
      <article class="metric metric--dark reveal"><strong>cXML + OCI</strong><span>Buyer sessions, carts, POs, store orders and invoices stay connected and visible.</span></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Keep exploring</span><h2>Go deeper into each step</h2></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/punchout/"><span>Platform</span><h3>PunchOut</h3><p>Understand the buyer session and cart return.</p><b>Explore →</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/purchase-orders/"><span>Platform</span><h3>Purchase Orders</h3><p>See how approved POs become Shopify orders.</p><b>Explore →</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/transactions/"><span>Platform</span><h3>Transactions</h3><p>See how the entire journey is monitored.</p><b>Explore →</b></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec soft" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>Questions suppliers usually ask</h2></div>
    <div class="faq reveal"><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does the buyer check out in Shopify?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. In a PunchOut session, the buyer returns the cart to procurement instead of completing normal Shopify checkout.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>When is the real order created?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>After internal approval, when the approved purchase order is received.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Can the whole transaction be tracked?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. PunchOut Central is designed around a connected transaction history.</p></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="page-cta">
  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <span class="ey">A bigger opportunity is waiting</span>
    <h2>See how simple enterprise procurement can feel.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Connect your first buyer and follow the order from session to invoice.</p>
    <div class="page-hero__actions">
      <a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Connect my first buyer →</a>
      <a class="btn secbtn" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
